# Glossary

## Core data model terms
| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **Source** | A warehouse connection (Postgres, BigQuery, etc.). Contains encrypted credentials. A dqt deployment can monitor many sources simultaneously. |
| **Monitored warehouse** | The user's actual data warehouse (a Source). dqt never writes to it. |
| **dqt metadata DB** | dqt's own control-plane Postgres. Stores configs, runs, incidents. Separate from monitored warehouses. |
| **Dataset** | A table or view within a Source. Has columns, row count, last sync time. |
| **Column** | A column within a Dataset. Has type, PII flag, classification, description, owner. |
| **Check** | A declarative binding of a Detector to a target (column/table/metric) with params and a baseline. |
| **Run / RunResult** | One execution of a Check. Produces a verdict (pass/warn/fail), a score, and plain_english. |
| **Incident** | Opened when a Run's verdict is warn or fail. Has a lifecycle (open→investigating→resolved→closed). |
| **Baseline** | The reference distribution or window a Detector fits against. Auto-fitted on first run. |

## Algorithm terms
| Plain English | Stat method | Slug |
|---|---|---|
| Distribution shape test | Shapiro-Wilk | `shapiro_wilk` |
| Normality test | Anderson-Darling | `anderson_darling` |
| Multimodality test | Hartigan's dip test | `hartigan_dip` |
| Drift: numeric column | Wasserstein-1 (earth-mover distance) | `wasserstein1` |
| Drift: numeric column | 2-sample KS test | `ks_2sample` |
| Drift: categorical column | Chi-square test | `chi_square` |
| Population Stability Index | PSI | `psi` |
| Outlier: single column | Modified Z-score (MAD-based) | `mad` |
| Outlier: tabular high-dim | ECOD | `ecod` |
| Time-series anomaly | STL residual | `stl` |
| Changepoint detection | BOCPD | `bocpd` |
| Causal discovery | PCMCI+ | `pcmci_plus` |
| Causal attribution | Shapley values | (not a detector — post-processing) |
| Sensitivity analysis | E-value | (annotation on DAG edges) |

## Lineage terms
| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **Column-level lineage** | Which upstream columns a downstream column was derived from. |
| **Blast radius** | The set of downstream columns/datasets affected if a given column has anomalies. |
| **Transform kind** | How an upstream column maps to a downstream one: `direct`, `aggregation`, `join`, `expression`. |
| **Confidence** | 0–1 score on a lineage edge. Lower for aggregations (identity lost), higher for direct column references. |

## Causality terms
| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **Driver-tree DAG** | The automatically-discovered directed graph of metric→metric influence. |
| **Proposed edge** | A causal edge suggested by the discovery pipeline but not yet human-confirmed. |
| **Confirmed edge** | A causal edge approved by a reviewer. Only confirmed edges are used for attribution. |
| **E-value** | Sensitivity of a causal edge to unobserved confounders. E-value < 1.5 → "fragile" badge. |
| **Shapley attribution** | Fair-share split of a metric's movement across upstream causal parents. |
| **Pearl's ladder** | Three levels of causal reasoning: association (observe), intervention (do), counterfactual (imagine). |
| **do-calculus** | Pearl's framework for reasoning about interventions: `do(X = x)` — what would happen if we forced X. |

## Governance terms
| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **Classification** | Data sensitivity level: `public`, `internal`, `confidential`, `restricted`. |
| **PII** | Personally Identifiable Information flag on a column. Redacted from logs and blocked from agent context. |
| **Freshness SLA** | Maximum allowed staleness for a dataset (e.g. "1h"). Violation opens an incident. |
| **Policy** | A declarative rule enforced by `PolicyEngine` at runtime. |
| **Audit log** | Append-only record of every actor+action+target in the system. |

## HITL terms
| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **HITL** | Human-in-the-Loop — human review of uncertain decisions before they enter the production system. |
| **Uncertainty sampling** | Prioritise items the model is least confident about. |
| **Query-by-committee** | Prioritise items where multiple detectors/models disagree most. |
| **hitl_labels** | The label store — every reviewed item becomes a training example here. |
